    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="0798" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.113 (Manchuria) Petroleum/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-25T12:00:00+09:00">April 25,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 25—3:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. Department’s 52, April 19, 5 p.m. I called on the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs today and made representations with a view to reinforcing oil companies
                    representations in Dairen, acting along the <pb facs="0799" n="709"
                        xml:id="pg709"/> lines of Department’s 89, October 6, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d608-f1"/> and 97, October 24 [<hi rendition="#italic">14</hi>], 4
                        p.m.<anchor n="94" xml:id="d608-f2"/> The Minister said he would interest
                    himself in the matter. I have informed my British colleague.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
